A||||7||fiero56||oil change and more power?!||||14||
Z||000000||fiero56||07-17-2000||06:28 PM||||My '88 2.8 with 162,000 miles has been clicking, clunking, knocking, etc the last month or two. I decided to change from the 5w30 I normally put  put in, and put in 10w40 instead. What a difference!!! The only sound I can hear(other than that sweet exhaust note) is the fuel rail happily clacking away. No lifter noise, no worn main bearing noise, nothing. <BR>I know this doesn't fix the problem, but it does cure the symptoms. Much better than I dared hope. <P>I do have one question though. I am a little crazy in the head(ask 87eco5 or WT III)but I am positive my 2.8 is giving me a significantly stronger kick in the pants when I punch the throttle. Am I crazy(well...more than I thought I was), or is it possible that my engine is belting out a few more ponies, due to a thicker oil? I don't know, maybe I was losing some compression in the cylinders, the valves didn't seal well, or maybe some swamp gas reflected off the moon, bounced the image back to earth, and little martian men came down in their space ship.......<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 07-17-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||GT Bastard||07-17-2000||08:21 PM||||If anything, you'd lose a couple horses from the added thickness of the oil.  Hardly noticeable.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||07-17-2000||08:56 PM||||The thicker the oil, the more resistance the engines moving parts will have.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||07-17-2000||09:09 PM||||Thicker oil... More power? Maybe less bleed off around worn bearings and lifters? Maybe more lift out of tired lifters??<P>Just some thoughts,<BR>Roy||||reg||7
Z||000004||gixxer||07-17-2000||09:29 PM||||My guess is your engine is a little loose and tired. The thicker oil is sealing the rings and guides a bit better. <BR>Or,... the old oil you drained out was thinned by fuel and water from blowby and condensation.<BR>Maybe a bit of both.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||07-17-2000||10:35 PM||||This engine doesn't burn any appreciable amount of oil between changes. ALL engines burn(lose)oil. On some though, it isn't noticed due to condensation, fuel, unburned contaminants, etc. This engine never smokes(except for what I suspect to be a leaky injector). It is getting a little loose in the bottom end, but the 10w40 got rid of the noise. The oil I changed out of it had just over 900 miles(still very clean), but I couldn't stand all the lifter and bearing noise, so I changed it out for thicker stuff. And I like it!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Patrick||07-18-2000||01:37 AM||||<BR>Does anyone (except me) add <B>STP</B> to their oil these days? Now that stuff is THICK.||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||07-18-2000||04:03 AM||||I added some CD2 to my dying 2.8 and it's pretty thick too!||||reg||1
